 "Its objections: two misleading but correct sentences in §6; an attribution, since Lemma 7.2 is called \"the padding lemma of van Doorn and Tang [22, Lemma 2.1]\" but its proof is sharper than theirs and rules out a case they treat separately; and ineffective thresholds in §8, harmless because only \"sufficiently large k\" is claimed. Its main remark is structural. §8 uses nothing from §§3–5, so Corollary 1.3, the lower bound of Corollary 1.2 (through v(k) ≤ kF(k) + 2) and Theorem 1.1 itself all survive any defect there; Bloom and van Doorn make the same observation. "
